in this lesson we're going to talk about  probability now probability is something  that you definitely want to know for the  math section of the act so let's define  probability so probability equals the  number of successes okay what you want  divided by the total possible outcomes  so the total number of things that could  occur so again probability is what you  want over the total  so let's look at a couple examples see  if you can pause the video for a moment  and see if you can solve these couple  examples we'll go through them together  so the first one says in a hat there are  slips of papers  numbered one through seven what is the  probability that if you reach in the hat  blindfolded that you pick an even number  okay so let's list out all the possible  things that could happen you could  basically get a one a two a three a four  a five a six or a seven right so it  looks like there's seven total possible  outcomes so that's the denominator but  how many even numbers are there there's  two there's four and there's six so  there's three even numbers so the  probability of picking an even number  would be three-sevenths  okay let's look at example number two  so this one they give us this region  here and it says if you throw a dart at  the board what is the probability that  you land in the shaded region assuming  that you hit the square you know region  so basically you're throwing a dart okay  you're going to land somewhere in this  square  okay  but what's the probability that you land  just in the shaded part okay now this  one is more like a geometric type of  probability problem and what you want  here is you want the area  of success okay that's the area that you  know that you're aiming for the area  that you want divided by the total  possible area so i'll just write total  area so in this case to find the shaded  region we're going to take the area of  the square which is 12 times 12 since  it's a square so that's 144  minus the part that we're removing which  is the circle now the circle has a  radius of 6 inches and the area of a  circle is pi r squared so this is going  to be pi times 6 squared  all divided by the total area which is  again the 144. so if we simplify this  down we get 144  minus 36 pi divided by 144 and that's an  exact answer now you can do it on your  calculator and you'll get a decimal  approximation but  oftentimes on the act they might just  leave it as an exact value or exact  answer like that so again probability  definitely something you want to know  for the ect easy questions to get right  i'll see you in the next lesson
 

